+- FINDING: on a delayed-allocation filesystem (ext4, XFS, APFS) ENOSPC surfaces at writeback, not at the accepting write. So the disagreement is reachable with NO error raised on either side: `io.Copy` reports the full length, the hasher agrees with the declared digest, and only `fstat` disagrees.
